**Data rules:**

- Every query is scoped by `user_id`. A global EF query filter is applied, and integration tests cover isolation.
- Task delete is a hard delete, keeping a `deleted` event without content.
- Account deletion cascades everything.
- A daily job inside the API purges expired transcripts, run outputs, and idempotency keys. It uses an `IHostedService` with a Postgres advisory lock, so no queue is needed.

## 9. Backend API contract (REST, `/api/v1`)

**Conventions:**

- JSON in camelCase. Errors use RFC 9457 Problem Details with a `code` field.
- `Idempotency-Key` is required on POSTs that create things.
- `If-Match: <version>` is used on task PATCH, returning 409 on conflict.
- Dates are ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` and instants are ISO UTC.

| Method & path                                                                             | Purpose                                                                                                            |
| :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `POST /auth/register` {email, password, inviteCode, timezone}                             | Register                                                                                                           |
| `POST /auth/login`, `POST /auth/logout`                                                   | Cookie session                                                                                                     |
| `GET /me`, `PATCH /me/settings`                                                           | Profile and settings                                                                                               |
| `GET /me/export`, `DELETE /me`                                                            | Export as JSON, delete account                                                                                     |
| `POST /transcriptions` multipart {audio, uploadId}                                        | STT. Returns `{id, status, text, durationMs, language}`                                                            |
| `POST /conversations`                                                                     | Start a session. The client starts a new one if the last message is more than 6 h old.                             |
| `GET /conversations?cursor=`, `GET /conversations/{id}`                                   | List, and detail including messages and pending tray                                                               |
| `DELETE /conversations/{id}`, `DELETE /conversations`                                     | Delete one or all                                                                                                  |
| `POST /conversations/{id}/messages` {clientMessageId, text?, transcriptionId?, inputMode} | Send a turn and get the reply and tray                                                                             |
| `PUT /messages/{id}` {text}                                                               | Edit, re-analyze, return the new tray                                                                              |
| `POST /messages/{id}/retry-analysis`                                                      | Re-run a failed analysis                                                                                           |
| `PATCH /proposal-items/{id}` {title?, scheduledDate?, priority?, estimateMinutes?}        | Edit an item before applying                                                                                       |
| `POST /proposal-items/apply` {itemIds[], rejectItemIds[]}                                 | Apply atomically. Returns `{applied:[{itemId, taskId, op}], skipped:[{itemId, reason}]}`                           |
| `GET /days/{date}`                                                                        | Tasks for the day, plus workload `{plannedMinutes, capacityMinutes, status}` and a carry-over count from yesterday |
| `GET /tasks?from&to&status&later=true`                                                    | Range query                                                                                                        |
| `POST /tasks` {title, scheduledDate?, priority?, estimateMinutes?, deadlineDate?}         | Manual create                                                                                                      |
| `PATCH /tasks/{id}`                                                                       | Edit fields                                                                                                        |
| `POST /tasks/{id}/complete`, `/reopen`, `/cancel`, `/reschedule` {toDate \| null}         | Lifecycle actions, each idempotent on state                                                                        |
| `DELETE /tasks/{id}`                                                                      | Delete                                                                                                             |
| `POST /tasks/move-unfinished` {fromDate, toDate \| null}                                  | Batch roll-over                                                                                                    |

