## 14. Phase tasks & acceptance criteria

**Phase 0 — Feasibility & evaluation harness (the go/no-go)**

- Tasks:
  - Write the golden set: 60 text cases, including §12.3. Record 40 audio clips from 4–6 speakers.
  - Create the solution skeleton with only `Domain`, `Application`, and `Eval`.
  - Implement DateResolver, Normalizer, the validation pipeline, and Policy, all pure.
  - Write ITurnAnalyzer adapters for 2 LLM vendors and ITranscriber adapters for 3 STT candidates.
  - Write prompt v1. Build the eval runner, which outputs a markdown report with the §12.2 metrics, per-case diffs, latency, and cost.
- Acceptance:
  - The eval runs with one command.
  - Domain unit tests are green, with the DateResolver table at 50+ rows or more.
  - A written STT and LLM selection appears in `decisions.md` with numbers.
  - The §12.2 gate is met on text input, or there is a documented plan with a re-test.
  - **If it misses badly, the product approach is revisited before building the UI.**

**Phase 1 — Backend foundation**

- Tasks:
  - `Infrastructure` + `Api` projects, plus Docker Compose with Postgres.
  - EF model and migrations for §8, including the pg_trgm extension.
  - Identity auth, invite codes, and the settings endpoint.
  - Task CRUD and lifecycle endpoints, the day endpoint with workload, and move-unfinished.
  - Idempotency middleware, Problem Details, rate limiter, and OpenTelemetry plus Serilog redaction.
  - OpenAPI document and CI with build, tests, and Testcontainers.
- Acceptance:
  - Integration tests cover user isolation, concurrent duplicate POSTs, If-Match conflicts, and lifecycle rules.
  - OpenAPI is published and the TS client generates cleanly.
  - `docker compose up` gives a working API locally.

**Phase 2 — Conversation & AI pipeline in the API**

- Tasks:
  - Conversations and messages endpoints, the context builder with aliases, and analysis run persistence.
  - Tray endpoints for edit and apply, message edit with supersede, and retry analysis.
  - The provider fallback chain and resilience policies.
- Acceptance:
  - Scenarios S1–S11, S13–S16, S18–S20, and S22–S24 pass as API-level tests with recorded model outputs.
  - The live eval still meets the gate.
  - Concurrent apply of the same items produces exactly one task each.

**Phase 3 — Voice capture & STT**

- Tasks:
  - The transcription endpoint with streaming upload to the provider and no disk persistence.
  - Vocabulary prompt biasing from task titles.
  - The client recorder state machine, IndexedDB chunk buffer, MIME negotiation, waveform, wake lock, and 5-minute cap.
- Acceptance:
  - Works on Chrome Android and iOS Safari, both in the browser and as an installed PWA.
  - Killing the tab mid-upload and reopening offers a retry with the audio intact.
  - S25 passes.
  - Stop → transcript p95 ≤ 5 s for a 60 s clip.

**Phase 4 — Frontend app**

- Tasks:
  - Auth screens, the Day view with Today/Tomorrow and date picker, task row and edit sheet, and optimistic toggles.
  - The Talk sheet with conversation, tray, inline edit, apply, clarifications, and the duplicate notice.
  - Settings & Privacy.
  - RTL and dark/light themes, reduced-motion support, and PWA manifest and service worker.
- Acceptance:
  - J1–J6 can be completed on a phone.
  - axe has no critical violations.
  - Playwright E2E passes the voice → tray → apply → Day view flow with a fake mic.
  - Arabic text renders correctly in all components.

**Phase 5 — Hardening & private beta**

- Tasks:
  - Retention purge job, export, and delete account.
  - Cost and latency dashboards and budget alerts.
  - Error-state polish and a privacy explainer.
  - Deploy with Caddy, the container host, and managed Postgres, plus a backup and restore drill.
  - Onboard 5–20 beta users with consent for evaluation sampling, and run a weekly eval-gap review.
- Acceptance:
  - S12, S17, and S21 pass, as do all §12.3 scenarios end-to-end.
  - A restore from backup is verified.
  - Two weeks of beta reach a tray acceptance rate of at least 80% and zero duplicate-task incidents.

## 15. Technical risks, open decisions & mitigations

**Risks:**

| Risk                                                | Likelihood / impact | Mitigation                                                                                                                                                   |
| :-------------------------------------------------- | :------------------ | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| STT quality on Egyptian code-switching is too low   | Med / High          | Phase 0 bake-off measured on downstream task F1. Vocabulary biasing. Editable transcript. The LLM is robust to transliteration. Self-hosted fine-tune in V2. |
| LLM over-extracts (invents or promotes aspirations) | Med / High          | Evidence check, commitment classes, Maybe section, review-before-apply, and the false-task metric in the gate.                                               |
| Wrong target on modify ops                          | Med / High          | Aliases, a clarification on ambiguity, explicit change rows, and nothing applied without a tap.                                                              |
| Off-by-one dates at night or across DST             | Med / Med           | A deterministic resolver with a large test table and explicit date display.                                                                                  |
| iOS PWA mic and MediaRecorder quirks                | High / Med          | Early device testing in Phase 3, an MP4 fallback, and a text input fallback.                                                                                 |
| Provider deprecation or price change                | Med / Med           | Ports and adapters, pinned versions, and the eval gate on swap.                                                                                              |
| Latency over 10 s on long clips                     | Med / Med           | 5-minute cap, the fastest acceptable STT, prompt caching, a small context, and the 2-step UI so progress is visible.                                         |
| Two-stack overhead slows a solo developer           | Med / Med           | Lean structure, generated types, same-origin deploy, and decision D-01 as an escape hatch.                                                                   |
| Privacy perception ("it listens to my feelings")    | Med / High          | No audio storage, a clear retention control, deletion, and no long-term memory in the MVP.                                                                   |
| Scope creep into a productivity super-app           | High / Med          | The non-goals list and the V1/V2 parking lot.                                                                                                                |

**Open decisions** (each has a default, so work is not blocked):

| ID   | Decision                               | Default                                                                                |
| :--- | :------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| D-01 | ASP.NET Core vs all-TypeScript backend | ASP.NET Core (preference). Switch if C# isn't a strength.                              |
| D-02 | STT provider                           | Decided by the Phase 0 bake-off                                                        |
| D-03 | LLM provider and model                 | Decided by the Phase 0 eval                                                            |
| D-04 | Task title language                    | English titles, with a setting for Arabic or match-speech                              |
| D-05 | Arabic UI in MVP?                      | No. English UI, RTL-safe content, Arabic UI in V1.                                     |
| D-06 | Auto-apply vs review                   | Review with one tap in the MVP. Opt-in auto-apply in V1 if precision is at least 0.95. |
| D-07 | Transcript retention default           | 30 days                                                                                |
| D-08 | Hosting provider and region            | A container host plus managed Postgres in an EU region                                 |
| D-09 | Beta access                            | Invite-only                                                                            |
| D-10 | Day boundary default                   | 04:00, user-adjustable                                                                 |

## 16. Recommended first implementation milestone

**Milestone 1 = Phase 0: "The Egyptian Arabic extraction proof", built inside the real backend solution.**

It produces a .NET solution with `Domain`, `Application`, and `Eval` projects only, plus:

- the golden dataset of 60 text cases and 40 audio clips
- DateResolver, Normalizer, validator, and policy with full unit tests
- adapters for 2 LLMs and 3 STT candidates
- a one-command eval report

**Why first:** Everything else is ordinary CRUD and UI that is known to be buildable. The only thing that can sink the product is whether a dialect conversation reliably becomes the right checklist. This milestone answers that in about a week of work, and none of it is throwaway, because it becomes the production domain core and the permanent regression gate.

**Done when:** The §12.2 gate is met on text, and the STT and LLM choices are recorded with evidence. Phase 1 starts after that.

